//
// #255 / @PLN9 — `source_dir()` returns the running program's OWN directory on
// every backend, the anchor source-relative asset loading builds on:
//   - `--interpret` / test runner → the source file's directory (set once at
//     parse time, the single home in `Parser::parse`);
//   - `--native` → the executable's directory (`current_exe().parent()`).
//
// The exact value differs per backend (source dir vs exe dir), so the portable
// cross-backend invariant asserted here is simply that it is POPULATED — the
// bug this guards was `source_dir()` returning "" under the test runners and
// natively.  The printed value makes the per-backend directory visible.
fn main() {
  sd = source_dir();
  assert(sd != "", "source_dir() must be populated on every backend (was empty)");
  print("source_dir=[{sd}]\n");
}
